We should maybe apply a blank line before and after long content, like thinking and highlighted code sections, and similar.
Currently dark theme backgrounds are much too bright, giving a washed-out feeling. Perhaps also use a hint of color. Nothing too obvious, just a subtle touch. Note that backgrounds for the dark theme must be properly dark, just as backgrounds for the light theme must be properly light, to preserve the contrast between text and background.
Make sure to have the highest contrast for standard black/white background for the most important parts, i.e. the agent result, tool use, input prompt, and final summary. Although they may each have their own definition of background in the theme configuration. Then we can use slightly grayer/tinted variants of that background for those other sub blocks. Just make sure that we still have great contrast in either case. Also note that highlighted code, may contain many different colors, therefore a more neutral background is probably a good idea. The intention is for a modern look, very readable.
Note that we want theming for both the Kvist and the agent-runner applications.
It'd be very nice if we could give the prompt area a very slight blue tint to the background.
The left gutter, for the thinking content doesn't share the gutter for soft-wrapped lines. Those lines are properly indented, but gets no gutter.
Please fix these issues, thanks


